<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Arthur Wellesley, 1st Duke of Wellington</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1769–1852</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Duke of Wellington, Arthur Wellesley</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Arthur Wellesley, 1st Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wellington">Wellington</a>, was a British general and statesman. After campaigns in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, he commanded the British and Portuguese armies in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peninsular-war">Peninsular War</a> from 1808, driving the French out of Portugal and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> by 1814. In 1815 he defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-waterloo">Waterloo</a> with the Prussians, and he later served twice as prime minister.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/arthur-wellesley-1st-duke-of-wellington.jpg" alt="Arthur Wellesley, 1st Duke of Wellington" width="320" height="437" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Thomas Lawrence · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sir_Arthur_Wellesley,_1st_Duke_of_Wellington.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
